diff --git a/docs/private-screen-share.md b/docs/private-screen-share.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..ad7f0544
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/private-screen-share.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# Private surfaces in monitor captures
+
+`hide_from_screen_share` is a boolean window and layer rule, disabled by default.
+It excludes the surface, its decorations, subsurfaces, popups, and closing animation
+from compositor screen captures. The capture shows the background and other windows
+behind it. Local display, focus, input, layout, and movement continue normally.
+
+This option requires running Hyprland built with this patch. Building the source
+does not update or restart an existing compositor session.
+
+Add a rule to `hyprland.lua`:
+
+```lua
+hl.window_rule({
+    name = "private-terminal",
+    match = { class = "^private-terminal$" },
+    float = true,
+    hide_from_screen_share = true,
+})
+
+hl.layer_rule({
+    name = "private-overlay",
+    match = { namespace = "^private-overlay$" },
+    hide_from_screen_share = true,
+})
+```
+
+For example, launch the terminal with `kitty --class private-terminal`.
+OBS should capture the monitor through the Wayland/PipeWire screen capture source.
+The rule applies to Hyprland's screencopy and image copy capture paths, including
+captures of monitor regions. Capturing a protected window directly is denied.
+
+The existing `no_screen_share` rule continues to draw a black rectangle.
+When both rules are enabled, `hide_from_screen_share` takes precedence.
+
+The capture scene is rendered separately only when a private surface or its closing
+animation is present on the captured monitor. This costs an additional scene render
+per captured frame. Separate blur resources prevent private pixels in the displayed
+scene from appearing through other captured surfaces' blur.
+
+Tiled windows still occupy their layout space, and layer surfaces still reserve their
+exclusive zones. Use floating windows or layers without an exclusive zone for an
+overlay that leaves the captured desktop layout intact. The shared cursor retains
+the capture client's normal cursor settings.
+
+For an upstream contribution, this new option also needs a separate Hyprland wiki PR.
